Lights are resampled over the shutter when it changes in the render delegate

A red sphere light moves along X, seen by a static camera. It's rendered by the render delegate with an
instantaneous shutter (sharp), then with a shutter of 1 frame (blurred), then instantaneous again (sharp). The
render delegate only knows the shutter once the camera is synced, so the lights must be resynced when it changes,
as in Solaris. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the blurred render is compared against the reference image.

See #2863 (ARNOLD-18309)

author: sebastien ortega

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
